          #SemiaddtiveStructureUnderlyingAdditiveInducesOriginalEnrichment.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Given an additive category according to def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
              which is induced on it via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductsAreBiproducts"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemiAdditivityInducesAbelianMonoidEnrichment"}
              from its underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiadditive+category"} semiadditive category
              structure coincides with the original enrichment.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By the proof of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductsAreBiproducts"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
              on any object in an additive category is the sum of the two projections:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\nabla_X \;\colon\; X \oplus X \overset{p_1 + p_2}{\longrightarrow} X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore (checking on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductsAreBiproducts"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon X \to Y
              we have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
