          %h2#references References
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 332
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-27950-4"} doi:10.1007/3-540-27950-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/kashiwara2.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An+Introduction+to+Homological+Algebra"} An Introduction to Homological Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139644136"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139644136
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug//otherpapers/weibel-hom.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#IntroductionToLinearCategories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to Linear Categories and Applications
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/mattearnshaw/lawvere/blob/192dac273e8bf352f307f87b9ec4fe8ef7dc85b9/pdfs/1992-introduction-to-linear-categories-and-applications.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lawvere-LinearCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on additive categories is around def. 4.3 of
          %ul
            %li#Beligiannis
              Apostolos Beligiannis,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of modules and Gorenstein rings
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://users.uoi.gr/abeligia/mathscand.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Formalization of additive categories as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations+of+mathematics"} univalent foundations of mathematics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"}> homotopy type theory
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unimath"}> unimath
              ,
              %em Additive categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://unimath.github.io/doc/UniMath/4dd5c17/UniMath.CategoryTheory.Additive.html"}> UniMath.CategoryTheory.Additive
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A characterisation of preadditive categories in terms of commutative monoids in cartesian multicategories is given in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
